opennyai_summary.decision:
3. During pendency of the present anticipatory bail application, the applicants and the informant have resolved their disputes.
Consent terms are filed before this Court on 3 May 2023.
The anticipatory bail application was adjourned to enable parties to comply with the consent terms.
Both the parties jointly state that consent terms are complied with.
4. In that view of the matter, I pass following order:
a) The anticipatory bail application is allowed;
a) In the event of arrest of the applicants in connection with C.R. No.21 of 2023 registered with Vimantal Police Station, Pune for offences punishable under Sections 406, 420 read with Section 34 of the Indian Penal Code, 1860, they be released on bail on furnishing P.R. Bond in the amount of Rs.5,000/- each with one surety in the like amount;
b) The applicants shall remain present before the investigating officer as and when called by the concerned investigating officer;
c) The applicants shall cooperate with the investigation and make himself available for interrogation whenever 43-aba669-2023.doc required;
5.
The anticipatory bail application stands disposed of in above terms.

